reverence for Latin and Greek classics.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nobel Literature Prize: How the winner is secretly chosen</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e535f6ba926f8cc6f897f395c8c0cd2f63527b7455ee53447544fc3dce8ea8d</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T13:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nobel-literature-prize-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151--42983d639d88.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nobel-literature-prize-how-the-winner-is-secretly-chosen/a-79564151?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Can Xue is considered one of this year's favorites; Margaret Atwood and Salman Rushdie are other strong contenders. But what goes on behind the scenes in the selection of the Nobel Prize in Literature?</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>France: Investigators recover 2 stolen Renoir paintings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:350c590aa10fa3f2d614d9af40294ac483fd0989f0ceafa7e946281ff50c466e</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:56Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T11:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-investigators-recover-2-stolen-renoir-paintings/a-79614538--ccdc42752159.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-investigators-recover-2-stolen-renoir-paintings/a-79614538?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thieves had initially taken four pieces with a value of over $10 million, but dropped two as they fled. Officials praised everyone that tracked down the paintings, but didn't reveal how they found them.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Two German officials shot dead during routine gun inspection in Bavaria; suspect arrested after overnight standoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1aca1963714c951089ccc00a5c2a0cf15cf5849d60ede32f2ab4892a3af106b</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T05:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/two-german-officials-shot-dead-during-routine-gun-inspection-in-bavaria-suspect-arrested-after-overn/live-79607225--1b63007f86d8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/two-german-officials-shot-dead-during-routine-gun-inspection-in-bavaria-suspect-arrested-after-overnight-standoff/live-79607225?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A routine inspection of legally owned firearms turned deadly in Bavaria. Police spent hours negotiating with an armed suspect before storming his home. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is China seeking to restrict Taiwan's cultural presence?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f50c3d29b37cb9145c366988e71b7d0ef87127c6a2f87db0cc296ba6bf7d04b3</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-china-seeking-to-restrict-taiwan-s-cultural-presence/a-79610947--71784c91bb83.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-china-seeking-to-restrict-taiwan-s-cultural-presence/a-79610947?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From coffee competitions to literature awards, Beijing appears to be working to limit Taiwan's international cultural and political impact.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Art for freedom: Maria Kalesnikava in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2043d32a6df72948d77fe32dfdaf71275b7b4234b5093387d97aab296fc849f5</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:23:44Z</updated><published>2026-10-09T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009--0f2314a86e67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/art-for-freedom-maria-kalesnikava-in-bonn/a-79612009?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Belarusian musician and civil rights activist Maria Kalesnikava held the keynote speech on the importance of art at the 2026 Beethovenfest in Bonn. She also visited DW.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>90s art scene in the UK: An international, edgy trendsetter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e23244eb90718a7e15fa3a230f62a5c1e6a74f2dbd475a6b47e9c4ce2c293be3</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:24:23Z</updated><published>2026-10-07T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777--d9e1246b3502.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/90s-art-scene-in-the-uk-an-international-edgy-trendsetter/a-79581777?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 1990s are remembered for Britpop and provocative fashion, but beyond the nostalgia, it was a decade of cultural experimentation and social change. Tate Britain's new exhibition looks past the familiar icons.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>This island in Kiribati could be the key to solve the Amelia Earhart mystery</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:302e340a53d94906ece0e4757305f79e219e87f28a2dd4c80e0db0008d59088e</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/this-island-in-kiribati-could-be-the-key-to-solve-the-amelia-earhart-mystery/a-79517455--5be17a2d6029.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/this-island-in-kiribati-could-be-the-key-to-solve-the-amelia-earhart-mystery/a-79517455?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nearly 90 years after US aviator Amelia Earhart vanished over the Pacific, a new expedition to the remote island of Nikumaroro hopes a lagoon anomaly could finally reveal the fate of her missing aircraft.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why music in Iran is more than just entertainment</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a7212532eb1eca78aee2fd8c7eeafeca2ef1c51dec710fa975959e54118e68e</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-08T05:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224--67cbee1305a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-music-in-iran-is-more-than-just-entertainment/a-79583224?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iranian authorities are trying to persuade prominent singers in exile to return home. While the state seeks to harness music as a political tool, music has also become a powerful expression of dissent and resistance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Campus Project 2026: Georgia takes center stage</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3e15c3335e47b8e426b2b04877a033d4df19722f687c164290b0f314cb1aa99f</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-23T09:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/campus-project-2026-georgia-takes-center-stage/a-79380639--efaea8063cd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/campus-project-2026-georgia-takes-center-stage/a-79380639?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Beethovenfest exchange project brings German and Georgian musical traditions together. And the reasons go beyond music.</summary><category term="NRS-Import" /></entry><entry><title>South Park satirist pushes for accountability in Cornell gang-rape lawsuit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f03fb09cce6ece0f0f30073e622fbc71d7859456d828058c4a4dc33b688aaf27</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T14:20:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382--e2bb4e991ce2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-park-satirist-pushes-for-accountability-in-cornell-gang-rape-lawsuit/a-79475382?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Writer Toby Morton is using a new website to amplify allegations in a high-profile sexual assault lawsuit involving seven Cornell students. The reopening of the case is causing an outcry on social media.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>DW shows solidarity with Georgians' commitment to democracy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c139cbac82408e24c5c6edbe65520f2c285d8bf4af02736e3c72af71fd2924c2</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-25T15:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dw-shows-solidarity-with-georgians-commitment-to-democracy/a-79432731--f6945c635292.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dw-shows-solidarity-with-georgians-commitment-to-democracy/a-79432731?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cultural and media professionals in Georgia remain under threat. A DW panel brings together insiders who share their hopes and fears.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Beethoven and Andy Warhol: Rebel icons on show in Bonn</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a7599c34a92443615c667a304762143efa5cc4bff318bb9bf65498cba565eab8</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944--59ad6d6535a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beethoven-and-andy-warhol-rebel-icons-on-show-in-bonn/a-79296944?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The new exhibition "Beethoven by Warhol" at the Beethoven House in Bonn presents the pop artist's late masterpiece: a picture of Ludwig van Beethoven. The exhibition shares the story of the work with the public.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Manchester City Premier League charges: What do they mean?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:52e402e1d6b19cf44ea7c69a31f5b009ccd023dbd2f76d19293dc0983ee266c2</id><updated>2026-10-09T15:22:55Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638--5f423a99075f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/manchester-city-premier-league-charges-what-do-they-mean/a-79485638?maca=en-rss-en-cul-2090-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since being bought by the UAE in 2008, Manchester City has become one of the world's most successful football clubs. A raft of serious financial charges threatens to undermine this and bring chaos to the Premier League.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
